{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1391872-a-2e-city","id":1391872,"title":"A 2E City","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-26T23:44:36-07:00","id":1391872,"title":"A 2E City","content":"So with all this time, I'm populating LA with monsters. So this thread is about mages. How does a society of mages function? I know there is the Consilium, and it has the diamond order, but what are the positions of power in it? And what about the free council? What positions do they have on a Consilium? Are there any Order specific positions that each city has? I'm going to re read the mage book again to get a feel for it, but I think that this community can make it easier to figure it all out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/13.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4793-hunterinthenight","name":"HunterInTheNight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"168"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T01:13:39-07:00","id":1391881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HunterInTheNight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1391872-a-2e-city#post1391872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So with all this time, I'm populating LA with monsters. So this thread is about mages. How does a society of mages function? I know there is the Consilium, and it has the diamond order, but what are the positions of power in it? And what about the free council? What positions do they have on a Consilium? Are there any Order specific positions that each city has? I'm going to re read the mage book again to get a feel for it, but I think that this community can make it easier to figure it all out.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's up to you to decide what the population of mages is in your game. Considering all the positions that have been described in all the order books etc there might be too many or to few, Each location might not have enough mages to fill every slot too. <br /> <br /> It might be a good exercise to go through the order books and list every position, I think I did it once and had it as a tinywiki file. <br /> <br /> Its a crap answer but it really does depend on how you want your area to work, lots of mages probably equals lots of conflict/friction over resources etc, deciding how many cabals and their size is probably the first thing you should do, then try filling out positions with whatever cabals you've created, you might find you need another cabal that covers x,y,z positions or might decide they don't even exist in this location.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T05:01:11-07:00","id":1391895,"title":"","content":"It all depends on the themes you want it to have. For example, what kind of person is the Hierarch ? A competent boss dealing with a balancing game ? A near tyrant that keeps everyone in line ? An incompetent mage that got there via political savvy ? A folk hero that was elected to an office he never wanted ?<br /> <br /> What kind of infrastructure each of the Orders have ? What kind of political influence do they have ? What are their political rivalries? For example, the Free Council could have the best quantum thaumaturgy lab in the world in this city, but little political power. Maybe its due to the Guardians gaining favor after suppressing an especially nasty Invader. How does that color the power dynamics and the Consilium's policies ? <br /> <br /> Does the Consilium have a budget for magical defenses, a command structure and a plan in case of an emergency? It might if the Arrows hold sway.<br /> <br /> How is the Lex Magicka enforced? What freedoms do Sentinels and Suspectors have ? Are they subtle or just kick in the door ? Does the Consilium believe in promoting Wisdom to prevent creating Rapt ? Or do they only solve the issue if it appears ?<br /> <br /> It all depends on the feel you want to create and the number of moving parts that seem right for your story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 05-27-2020, 08:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T08:52:16-07:00","id":1391956,"title":"","content":"Los Angeles actually gets a write-up in the Mage 2e book: politically LA is weird in that it has a large Assembly with members of the Diamond Orders and a large Consilium that includes members of the Free Council; this implies LA has a lot of Mages (certainly over one hundred Pentacle mages), but the book references Orange County and Oxnard (in Ventura County, where I live!) as being areas LA mages live (which tracks with mundane reality, there are lots of people that commute from Ventura to LA).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T09:08:55-07:00","id":1391960,"title":"","content":"In regards to the population size, This is a multi splat city, I already have a hundred vampires and plans to quadruple that number. I've got ten werewolf packs. So I'm not sure how many mages can be sustained in such a city.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/13.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4793-hunterinthenight","name":"HunterInTheNight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"168"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T09:18:26-07:00","id":1391964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HunterInTheNight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1391872-a-2e-city?p=1391960#post1391960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In regards to the population size, This is a multi splat city, I already have a hundred vampires and plans to quadruple that number. I've got ten werewolf packs. So I'm not sure how many mages can be sustained in such a city.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The simple answer is &quot;As many as you need.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T09:38:54-07:00","id":1391972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HunterInTheNight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1391872-a-2e-city?p=1391960#post1391960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In regards to the population size, This is a multi splat city, I already have a hundred vampires and plans to quadruple that number. I've got ten werewolf packs. So I'm not sure how many mages can be sustained in such a city.</div> </div> </div> </div>Supernaturals don't really compete for resources between splats.<br /> <br /> Vampires need a human population, more humans can sustain more vampires, and the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greater_Los_Angeles\" target=\"_blank\">Greater Los Angeles area</a> has over 18 million people.<br /> <br /> Werewolves need spirits, and spirits need essence. How much essence is available to spirits is entirely up to you.<br /> <br /> Mages need Mysteries, and LA is replete with weird shit to investigate.<br /> <br /> Unless you end up with tens of thousands of supernaturals it'll hardly even be a blip on the actual population.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T10:03:14-07:00","id":1391980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1391872-a-2e-city?p=1391972#post1391972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolves need spirits, and spirits need essence. How much essence is available to spirits is entirely up to you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolves do not need spirits, and unless something has gone horribly wrong Essence tends to be more common than air.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HunterInTheNight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1391872-a-2e-city#post1391872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So with all this time, I'm populating LA with monsters. So this thread is about mages. How does a society of mages function? I know there is the Consilium, and it has the diamond order, but what are the positions of power in it? And what about the free council? What positions do they have on a Consilium? Are there any Order specific positions that each city has? I'm going to re read the mage book again to get a feel for it, but I think that this community can make it easier to figure it all out.</div> </div> </div> </div>As noted above, the mage core has a Los Angeles write-up, though it won't give you a strict population count. The best book on how a consilium is set up is first edition's <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/3137/Sanctum--Sigil\" target=\"_blank\">Sanctum &amp; Sigil</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-27-2020, 01:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T11:01:52-07:00","id":1391997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1391872-a-2e-city?p=1391980#post1391980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Werewolves do not need spirits, and unless something has gone horribly wrong Essence tends to be more common than air.</div> </div> </div> </div>While you could theoretically have a werewolf game that had nothing to do with spirits and never involved the <i>Hsil</i> that would be a very strange werewolf game.<br /> <br /> And, yes, essence is very common, I never said it wasn't, that doesn't mean it's freely available to spirits. Aluminum oxide is incredibly easy to come by, and yet we are not all replete with sapphires and rubies.<br /> <br /> The point was to highlight that Werewolves, Vampires, &amp; Mages (and by extrapolation, other splats) do not have overlap where the existence of one would compete with the existence of another.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T18:23:38-07:00","id":1392086,"title":"","content":"Ah but everything overlaps, even if only the fact that too many monster in one area attracts too many hunters to make society sustainable. Werewolves draw Thyrus. Vampires draw death and dependence spirits for werewolves to deal with. Prometheans and geists have good reason to avoid areas where certain werewolf tribes are dominant. Beasts throw everything into disarray. By the very nature of how each monster has to interact with the world, it messes with other types, even if they don't compete for things. So this being a multi splat city means that there would be less mages than a pure mage city because you can't always stay out of everyone elses way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/13.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4793-hunterinthenight","name":"HunterInTheNight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"168"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-28T08:04:50-07:00","id":1392195,"title":"","content":"I'm currently dealing with something very similar to what the OP is doing. I am going to be running a MtAw 2e game set in Dallas/Ft Worth. I don't want it to be a cross over game, but I do want &quot;official&quot; versions of Vampires, Werewolves and Changelings. I have decided that each Caucus will have about 15 members. Wanting the Consilium to consist of bout 15 Cabals....around 75 mages in Dallas area. Now I am having Fort Worth be its own group of mages, 80% Seers of the Throne. Between them in Arlington, basically &quot;neutral territory&quot;, will be the Changeling Court(s?). The Metroplex will be in a &quot;state of Cold War&quot; between the Mage factions. The other splats will be &quot;minor players&quot; who assist and/or oppose the Dallas Consilium mages. Hoping that info about what I am developing can help you make some decisions and flavors for your Setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12207-mahjemm01","user":"Mahjemm01","date":". 05-28-2020, 11:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12207-mahjemm01","name":"Mahjemm01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-28T09:13:37-07:00","id":1392214,"title":"","content":"That's like a third the pop of LA. Hmmm. Rounding it down because you're mage focused. That helps, thanks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/13.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4793-hunterinthenight","name":"HunterInTheNight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"168"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T14:26:21-07:00","id":1394435,"title":"","content":"Something that came to mind the other day, the minor template. By that I mean, ghouls, wolf blooded, promixi and sleepwalkers, etc. You might want to tone down the number of Supernatural beings because of that. 8 million people, and you are having 200 vampires (just a example). Then there would like 600+ ghouls. Then take that and add in the number of werewolves and wolf blooded. And same for mages. And for Changelings. And etc. That could add up to being ALOT more supernaturals then you originally wanted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12207-mahjemm01","name":"Mahjemm01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T07:46:18-07:00","id":1395344,"title":"","content":"On the &quot;Too many titles for the number of Mages&quot; problem, I generally find that its fun to have NPCs wear multiple hats. Its realistic considering you probably aren't going to want dozens of master mage NPCs in a single city and it tends to add lots of opportunities to add depth and unusual political intrigue to their interactions. The Consilium Herald might also be a Ladder Factotum and the leader of a major local Legacy for example.<br /> <br /> This is doubly true at the top end. In every game I have run or played in the local Hierarch has doubled as the leader of his local order caucus and its not unusual for the Councillors of the various paths to include the local Epopts/Adamant Sages etc.<br /> <br /> If your looking for the various titles and their job descriptions the &quot;Mage Society&quot; section of the 2e Corebook has a surprisingly thorough overview of them all, which should be plenty for a crossover game/setting outline. The 1e Order books are great for additional details and I think someone already mentioned Sanctum and Sigil.<br /> <br /> Leaving a few positions notably vacant is also a fun hanging plot thread if you have Mage PCs who might be interested in claiming those jobs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6230,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","user":"Katana1515","date":". 06-09-2020, 10:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-10T04:14:27-07:00","id":1395575,"title":"","content":"I see others have come up with some good advice, but I'll add some of my own:<br /> <br /> - In LA you can get away with a really high population of supernatural individuals, higher than you could reasonably stat properly, actually. Taking into account inner city /suburb population, transient population and some rural odd members, you can go crazy researching and creating NPCs. What you really need is to answer two questions: How cosmopolitan/political is my chronicle going to be? and, What are the themes and mood I'm trying to portray? The answers to these questions would put some boundaries to your design, while allowing you to focus on what really matters for the chronicle.<br /> <br /> - What gamelines/creatures are you intending to fully describe, which are only going to be in the background and which are non-existant in YOUR Chronicles of Darkness? Again, talking about the games your players are really going to make PCs for can help you bring up the main themes and conflicts of the chronicle. You should build your setting around that, and not the other way around, IMO.<br /> <br /> - What degree of interaction between supernatural communities are you aiming for? Each CofD gameline exists in the same shared universe, but the modular nature of these games means that there is little to none official lore regarding crossover and/or multisplat games, barring the upcoming Contagion Chronicles. Are each supernatural community aware of the other ones in the area? Is any community in conflict with any other? Are there any isolationist communities? Is there a non-aggresion pact in place? What about Tier 1 groups? Is it common to find multisplat groups and/or factions? Is there a goberning, arbitral and/or legislative body regulating interactions between each supernatural faction in the city?<br /> <br /> I have my own example to show. My chronicle is set in New Orleans, with a heavy emphasis on Mages and Vampires over other splats. No splat is absent from the setting, but Demons and the God-Machine are fairly in the background, and Beasts are not a playable option at the moment. I was aiming at a Tier 2 game, with some local politics that are more about personal ambitions and vendettas than any overarching faction's agenda. In New Orleans all communities are more or less aware of each other, and multisplat parties are not unheard of, though most such groups are usually temporary alliances more than established parties. Althoug there is no direct competition between splats, there are certain &quot;niches&quot; that each community is known for, which the other factions are adviced to stay clear of them. Vampires have their bloody fingers in most high-level politics and financial companies; some of the bayous are under direct protection of certain werewolf packs; changelings are very discreet and are only seen with any regularity only in certain points around the city, especially in the French Market; mages oversee several mysteries in an around the city, but tend to avoid the French Quarter and the Superdome to avoid clashing with the vampires there. Oh, and the local Beasts have made themselves a reputation for keeping the peace among the communities and serve as a go-between among factions, but only because they viciously hunt and devour any serious offender to the status quo.<br /> <br /> Well, there is more to that, but I hope this helps you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","name":"Zooroos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}